{
  "_how_to_use": "PRIVATE analysis file for one opportunity. Save as <store>/private/analysis/<OPP-id>.json (never in the public repository). Every number is {value, ref}: ref = an evidence ID (EVD-…), PRIVATE:<package_id>/<fact key>, or ASSUMPTION with a note. A value that differs from its referenced record needs a note explaining the derivation. Then run: node desk/_tools/ingest.mjs report --store <store> --id <OPP-id> FIN-2 conventions: payment times t are in years from today and may be decimals (0.25 = month 3; monthly instalments can be listed one by one); rent.gross_annual is the gross rent of the FIRST RENTED YEAR (the year after delivery), not today's rent; ROI is a total over the horizon, IRR is the annual rate; in TRY always add views.inflation (and, for a foreign investor, views.home_currency) — nominal TRY figures alone overstate the return. Every fx row needs ref = the evidence ID (or PRIVATE fact) of that rate, with the same value and date.",
